Rehearsal: Meet FixQuest AI. Turn everyday home problems into interactive repair adventures. This recording uses an Amazon Fire tablet.
Rehearsal: Three rooms, three quests: a dripping tap, a slow sink, and a sticking door. Every action works with directional controls.
Rehearsal: Start with a model tap. Observe the scenario, consider the clues, and learn when to stop for qualified help.
Rehearsal: The focus ring shows the selected answer. Use the D-pad to move and Select to make a choice.
Rehearsal: A wrong answer is a chance to learn. The guide gives a contextual nudge, and you can try again.
Rehearsal: QuestGuide offers curated guidance offline. It is deterministic, not live generative AI. Prompts can use an installed offline system voice.
Rehearsal: First, identify where the drip appears. Observation comes before guessing at a hidden problem.
Rehearsal: The model explains a likely cause, while recognising that different tap designs use different parts.
Rehearsal: Original illustrations and a simple toolkit make each decision visual. Here, choose a fitted spanner with a protective cloth.
Rehearsal: Now build a safe sequence in the model: isolate the water, verify flow has stopped, then replace the matching washer.
Rehearsal: The puzzle rewards the order of the checks. If isolation is uncertain, stop and get help.
Rehearsal: Mission complete. Earn a badge and experience points. The best completed result is saved locally, and retries remain part of learning.
Rehearsal: Another room brings another interaction. Align the virtual door marker with its target. This is a simulation, not a diagnosis.
Rehearsal: Small remote movements bring the model into alignment. The explanation reminds us that real doors can stick for several reasons.
Rehearsal: Knowing when a problem needs professional assessment is part of the game. Complete a quest to unlock its badge.
Rehearsal: XP and badges stay on this device. Replaying can improve a best score, without counting the same mission again and again.
Rehearsal: No login, backend, or API key. FixQuest AI makes home knowledge a shared adventure. Fire TV demo footage is still required.
Tablet rehearsal captured; not Fire TV submission evidence.
